---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const seo = {
  page_description: "Learn about uDocumentView's mission to provide fast, secure, zero-footprint document viewing for everyone.",
  open_graph_type: "website"
};
---
<Layout title="About Us | uDocumentView" seo={seo}>
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-8">About uDocumentView</h1>
    <div class="prose prose-slate prose-lg max-w-none">
      <p>We believe that viewing a document shouldn't require installing bulky software, creating an account, or surrendering your privacy.</p>

      <h2>Our Mission</h2>
      <p>uDocumentView was built to solve a simple problem: opening files quickly and safely. Whether you are on a public computer, a restricted corporate network, or just don't have Microsoft Office installed, we provide a secure bridge to your content.</p>

      <h2>Zero Footprint Philosophy</h2>
      <p>Traditional document viewers upload your files to a server, process them, and often keep them for "caching" or "analytics." We take a different approach. We leverage modern browser technologies to parse and render documents locally whenever possible. When server-side processing is strictly required, it is done entirely in ephemeral memory. The moment you close the tab, the data is gone.</p>

      <h2>Supported Formats</h2>
      <p>We are constantly expanding our format support. Currently, we specialize in:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/reference/formats/pdf/">Portable Document Format (PDF)</a></li>
        <li><a href="/reference/formats/docx/">Microsoft Word (DOCX)</a></li>
        <li><a href="/reference/formats/xlsx/">Microsoft Excel (XLSX, CSV)</a></li>
        <li><a href="/reference/formats/pptx/">Microsoft PowerPoint (PPTX)</a></li>
        <li>OpenDocument Formats (ODT, ODS)</li>
        <li>Standard Text (TXT, RTF)</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Need to get in touch? <a href="/contact/">Contact us here.</a></p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
